      "text": "This \"lifestyle centre\" is an open-air mall with a mix of retail, dining, and entertainment.\n\n**Why scout here**\n\nCF Shops at Don Mills is a significant commercial hub that aims to create a welcoming, walkable urban setting with a variety of amenities.\n\nThe presence of numerous restaurants and cafes, including some with family-friendly options like Jack Astor's, suggests a potential audience for a new café.\n\nThe centre has previously hosted family-oriented activities and has amenities like family washrooms and a nursing room.\n\nAn outdoor playground exists within the Shops at Don Mills, though its placement has been noted as somewhat removed from the main foot traffic.\n\n**Reasons to hesitate**\n\nWhile there's an outdoor playground at CF Shops at Don Mills, one source describes its location as an \"afterthought,\" away from the central square and main foot traffic.\n\nThe concept of a café with an *indoor* playground has existing examples in Toronto, such as The Willow Play Cafe in the Junction neighbourhood and Pinocchio Play Café in Lawrence Park.\n\nCF Shops at Don Mills also features various restaurants and cafes such as Eataly, Joey Don Mills Grill/Lounge, McEwan, Scaddabush Italian Kitchen, Anejo Restaurant, Nome Izakaya, Pablo's Coffee House, Jack Astor's Bar & Grill, and Tim Hortons.\n\nEataly offers Italian classics for all ages and includes both grab-and-go and seated restaurant options.\n\nJack Astor's Bar & Grill is noted as a kid-friendly option.\n\nMany offer dine-in, takeaway, and delivery.\n\n**Access and local context**\n\nThe location is at Don Mills Road and Lawrence Avenue East.\n\nCF Shops at Don Mills is accessible by car and public transit, with free parking available in a multi-level garage.\n\nThe shopping centre is described as an open-air lifestyle centre with storefronts facing internal streets, similar to a regular neighbourhood retail area.\n\nThe Aga Khan Museum is located approximately one and a half kilometres southeast of the Shops at Don Mills.\n\nEvaluate existing indoor play offerings in the immediate vicinity of Don Mills Road, considering the upcoming Jolly Bubble Indoor Playground.",
